# KISTI-6 HANGANG: 4x GH200 per node, Slingshot (4 NICs, dragonfly), Slurm with pyxis/enroot.
# Loaded by sites/load.sh; a variable already set (environment, site.env) wins.
# Site notes: https://docs-ksc.gitbook.io/hangang-user-guide and the swiss-ai kisti-docs.

# Slurm. intTest is the partition KISTI dedicated to us (no per-user job limits); every job
# must name a partition, request GPUs with --gres and carry a --comment tag (see `showappl`).
# Nodes are allocated whole; --exclusive also lifts the single-node limits on CPU/memory flags.
: "${ACCOUNT:=in0138}"
: "${DEFAULT_PARTITION:=intTest}"
: "${RUN_PARTITION:=intTest}"
: "${GPUS_PER_NODE:=4}"
: "${SBATCH_EXTRA=--gres=gpu:4 --exclusive --comment=field=nlp;appl=pytorch}"
: "${EXCLUDE_NODES=}"

# Filesystems. /scratch is purged (files unaccessed for 15 days) and must be the submit
# directory; /home01 is backed up, so the source clones live there.
: "${SCRATCH:=/scratch/${USER}}"
: "${PROJECTS_DIR:=${HOME}/projects}"

# Containers: pyxis flags built from the stack's edf.toml.template by backends/nemo-rl/container.sh.
: "${CONTAINER_RUNTIME:=pyxis}"
# KISTI: LL128 gives wrong inter-node all-reduce results on HANGANG; their recommended set.
# SLURM_NETWORK (read by ray.sub's srun): the site runs libfabric with FI_CXI_RDZV_PROTO=alt_read,
# which wants rendezvous GET disabled on the Slurm side, as in KISTI's own multi-node scripts.
# UV_DEFAULT_INDEX: the Apertus 2 image points uv at CSCS's JFrog PyPI mirror, unreachable here
# (pydeps.sh installs its overlay with uv).
# NRL_HBM_BIND_CPU: the NVIDIA driver here (570) moves the CPU-offloaded optimizer's host memory
# into the trainer GPU's HBM despite srun --mem-bind (it honours only per-mapping mbind); with
# AdamW about 19 GiB per GPU landed there after the first optimizer step and the next backward
# ran out of memory (job 1171437). NeMo-RL's hbm_spill binds those mappings to the CPU nodes
# after setup and after every optimizer step (job 1173010: 0 GiB on HBM). It only acts on
# CPU-offloading optimizers.
SITE_ENV=(NCCL_PROTO=^LL128 FI_PROVIDER=cxi NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 SLURM_NETWORK=disable_rdzv_get
          UV_DEFAULT_INDEX=https://pypi.org/simple NRL_HBM_BIND_CPU=1)
# strtok() with per-thread state, preloaded into every container process (built by container.sh).
# libfabric's CXI provider reads the job's Slingshot service from SLINGSHOT_DEVICES and
# SLINGSHOT_SVC_IDS with strtok(), and UCCL's proxy threads parse them at once; a misread NIC
# falls back to a lookup by user ID, which finds nothing as root in the container, and UCCL
# aborts with "fi_domain failed: Function not implemented" (jobs 1172975, 1173381, 1173383,
# always on cxi1, the first NIC that needs a second strtok() call).
SITE_PRELOAD=(backends/nemo-rl/strtok_ts.c)

# Read-only shared copies in the group's scratch (hanint02), used in place: nothing is copied
# and nothing is written there. No registry: the JFrog images of Alps are not reachable.
: "${SHARED:=/scratch/hanint02}"
# The site config mounts /scratch, /home01, /apps and /appsdata into every container, but
# ray.sub runs pyxis with --no-container-mount-home; mount what jobs use explicitly, as the
# first working runs here did (home: this repository and the clones; scratch; the shared copies).
SITE_MOUNTS=("${HOME}" "${SCRATCH}" "${SHARED}")
: "${APERTUS2_IMAGE_MASTER:=${SHARED}/images/nemo-rl-apertus2-cfcfede4-ucclfix.sqsh}"
: "${APERTUS2_IMAGE_WORK:=${APERTUS2_IMAGE_MASTER}}"
: "${APERTUS2_REGISTRY=}"
# Chonk HF export with the modeling code already added; stage_model.sh links it into scratch.
: "${CHONK_MODEL_SRC:=${SHARED}/models/apertus2-chonk-lc-iter3576}"
: "${CHONK_MODEL_STAGE:=link}"
